---
description: Conventions for the Recharge mobile app (Kotlin Multiplatform, Android and iOS)
globs: ["**/*.kt", "**/*.kts", "**/*.xml", "**/*.swift", "**/*.sq"]
alwaysApply: true
---
- Kotlin Multiplatform with Compose Multiplatform (Material 3), Ktor, kotlinx.serialization, SQLDelight, multiplatform-settings, kotlinx-datetime.
- Everything goes in `shared/src/commonMain` unless it needs a platform API. No `java.*`, `android.*` or `platform.*` imports in commonMain.
- Platform differences go behind `PlatformServices` (one implementation in androidMain, one in iosMain). Do not add `expect`/`actual`.
- Objects are created and connected in `AppGraph`. No DI framework.
- Layers: ui (Composable + ViewModel) -> domain (use cases, models) -> data (api, repository). Domain has no UI or HTTP imports.
- ViewModels expose one immutable StateFlow<UiState>. Composables are stateless; anything that must survive rotation or process death uses rememberSaveable.
- Money and payment: one Idempotency-Key per order attempt, kept with rememberSaveable in PaymentRoute. Ignore taps while processing. A lost payment response is "pending, checking status", never "failed, try again".
- Server state is the source of truth. The status screen always reads the API.
- All user-visible text in composeResources/values (en) and values-de. Placeholders are positional (%1$d). No hardcoded colors. Touch targets >= 48dp.
- Network: every call goes through `ApiClient`. Retry only idempotent requests. Never log request bodies or phone numbers.
- Telemetry: record through TelemetryRecorder only. No personal data in props. Behavioral events need consent; the recorder enforces it.
- Recommendation is optional: any failure or timeout means "no badge", never an error screen.
- Tests go in `shared/src/commonTest` with kotlin.test, coroutines-test, Turbine and Ktor MockEngine (see `FakeServer`). No MockK or JUnit-only APIs. Ask before adding dependencies.
